# Almost empty on purpose.
#
# All of this shield's *defaults for zmk-rgbled-widget* live in Kconfig
# *fragments* instead:
#
#   cornix_indicator.conf                    - shared by both halves
#   boards/cornix_left_nrf52840_zmk.conf     - central (left) half LEDs
#   boards/cornix_right_nrf52840_zmk.conf    - peripheral (right) half LEDs
#   boards/cornix_ph_left_nrf52840_zmk.conf  - left half in dongle mode
#
# They are merged after the board defconfig and before the user's
# ZMK_CONFIG/<board>.conf, so a user can still override any of them.
# Putting them here instead would require the RGBLED_WIDGET_* symbols to
# exist, i.e. it would hard-fail any build where zmk-rgbled-widget is not in
# config/west.yml.  That is not a theoretical worry: Zephyr sources *every*
# shield's Kconfig.defconfig in *every* build (zephyr/Kconfig.zephyr sources
# `boards/shields/*/Kconfig.defconfig` by glob, before the module Kconfigs are
# even read) - which is also why everything below is wrapped in
# `if SHIELD_CORNIX_INDICATOR`.
#
# The symbols that *are* defined here are this shield's own, so they are safe:
# they name no module symbol, and the CMakeLists.txt that acts on them checks
# for CONFIG_RGBLED_WIDGET_WS2812 in CMake, where an undefined symbol is
# simply false.

if SHIELD_CORNIX_INDICATOR

config CORNIX_INDICATOR_LEDS_ON_USB
	bool "Keep the status LEDs lit while the half is USB-powered"
	default y
	help
	  zmk-rgbled-widget shows every status for a fixed time
	  (CONN_*_DURATION_MS, BATTERY_BLINK_MS) and then lets the LED go dark,
	  after which RGBLED_WIDGET_EXT_POWER_TIMEOUT_MS cuts the WS2812 rail.
	  That is what you want on battery and not what you want on a cable.

	  With this enabled, src/leds_on_usb.c re-asserts the current state with
	  a zero duration whenever zmk_usb_is_powered() is true, which is what
	  the widget treats as "persistent": the connectivity LED keeps showing
	  the active output (cyan for USB, the profile colour for BLE) and the
	  battery LED keeps showing charge state (green pulse while charging,
	  steady green once full), and the rail is never cut.

	  On battery nothing changes: every code path in that file returns
	  immediately when USB power is absent.

	  Needs RGBLED_WIDGET_WS2812 and a USB device stack; without either, the
	  shield's CMakeLists.txt compiles nothing and this symbol is inert.

endif # SHIELD_CORNIX_INDICATOR

# vim: set ft=kconfig:
